# Windows .bat/.cmd files must always check out with CRLF line endings --
# some Windows tools (and older cmd.exe behaviour) are picky about it, and
# without this pinned explicitly, Git's own line-ending auto-detection can
# disagree with itself between machines/checkouts. That mismatch is exactly
# what produced a real "local changes would be overwritten by merge" error
# on scripts/run_webapp.bat for a Windows user who never touched the file --
# Git's autocrlf conversion on checkout looked like an uncommitted edit.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
